    <content type="html">&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/TimoStahl/kanboard_plugin_bigboard&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;img&#xA;        src=&#34;https://shots.wayl.one/shot/?url=https://github.com/TimoStahl/kanboard_plugin_bigboard&amp;height=450&amp;width=800&amp;scaled_width=800&amp;scaled_height=450&amp;selectors=&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;shot of post - TimoStahl/kanboard_plugin_bigboard: A Kanboard that can display multiple projects&#34;&#xA;        height=450&#xA;        width=800&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s my thought on &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/TimoStahl/kanboard_plugin_bigboard&#34;&gt;TimoStahl/kanboard_plugin_bigboard: A Kanboard that can display multiple projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I use kanboard to keep myself focused at home - it&amp;rsquo;s great because it&amp;rsquo;s simple enough but does have complex features (that I largely don&amp;rsquo;t need). It&amp;rsquo;s got a great REST API for integrations and looks decent.&#xA;Well today I discovered &amp;ldquo;plugins&amp;rdquo; for it - and those make it even better - tis BigBoard plugin gives me a way better view of my projects, letting me minimize the ones I don&amp;rsquo;t need to look at &amp;ldquo;right now&amp;rdquo; but not using any weird search filters or anything - a simple intuitive &amp;ldquo;big board&amp;rdquo; of my projects and their subsequent tasks.&#xA;Very excited to find some more useful plugins!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;admonition note&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p class=&#34;admonition-title&#34;&gt;Note&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is one of [[ my-thoughts ]]. I picked this up from &lt;a href=&#34;https://waylonwalker.com&#34;&gt;Waylon Walker&lt;/a&gt;(&lt;a href=&#34;https://thoughts.waylonwalker.com&#34;&gt;https://thoughts.waylonwalker.com&lt;/a&gt;). It&amp;rsquo;s a short note that I make about someone else&amp;rsquo;s content online.  Learn more about the process &lt;a href=&#34;/thoughts/&#34; class=&#34;wikilink&#34; data-title=&#34;Thoughts&#34; data-description=&#34;My thoughts are found at my thoughts feed&#34; data-date=&#34;2025-06-09&#34; data-preview=&#34;My thoughts are found at my thoughts feed&#34;&gt;Thoughts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;</content>
